ation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{y/2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)/2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\sqrt{x}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ 1 & =2\\sqrt{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{y/2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)/2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & =\\frac{2}{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true.* Therefore, the function $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{y/2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)/2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{-1/2})}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{{x}^{-1/2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{x} & =2\\sqrt{x} \\\\ -1 & =2x\\sqrt{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281414 13194139534191 true] [17592186281413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281415 13194139534191 true] [17592186281413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281416 13194139534191 true] [17592186281413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281417 13194139534191 true] [17592186281413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281418 13194139534191 true] [17592186281413 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534191 true] [17592186281413 1041 "selection" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281413 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281418 13194139534191 true] [17592186281413 1110 #uuid "14ce3d7f-290b-5336-8578-d6aa19601a4a" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281414 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534191 true] [17592186281414 1111 #uuid "c3f7892e-2376-5f4d-ab2f-2fc9850117bf" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281415 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281415 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534191 true] [17592186281415 1111 #uuid "c58e99f4-4cc4-5dd5-b7e6-5456542cb904" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281416 1034 "I only" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281416 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534191 true] [17592186281416 1111 #uuid "91627b8a-627f-5c2e-a6ff-0ff3d52ce635" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281417 1034 "III only" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534191 true] [17592186281417 1111 #uuid "24d20f25-8bb9-5064-94e6-5bca9c6df55b" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281418 1034 "II only" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534191 true] [17592186281418 1111 #uuid "1aea66b2-c4cb-5cf9-b060-bc56cab96f27" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281419 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281420 13194139534191 true] [17592186281419 1089 "q-141098" 13194139534191 true] [17592186281419 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534191 true] [17592186281419 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d